DeepSalviaDB Code, Data, and Model Notice
Copyright 2026 DeepSalviaDB contributors

DeepPPI uses external protein sequences and interaction data. The parts of
the frozen dataset originating from STRING v12.0 are used under STRING's
CC BY 4.0 terms. Credit STRING and indicate any changes:
https://string-db.org/cgi/access?footer_active_subpage=licensing
Material from other providers remains subject to their original terms.

The bundled ProMoAI train, development, and test CSV files contain sequences
derived from the DSS3 genome. Their inclusion does not change the terms of
the source genome or annotation resources. The bundled TMC-Miner count,
expression, and metabolite-intensity tables likewise remain subject to
the terms of their original data providers. Credit those providers when
using the datasets.

ProMoAI uses the Plant DNA LLMs / PDLLM foundation models Plant DNAGPT-BPE
and Plant DNAGPT-6mer from Zhang Tao Lab. This project trains classification
heads based on those models. The original PDLLM code and foundation models
belong to their authors and are subject to the upstream CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
terms. This repository does not relicense the foundation models or fine-tuned
weights containing their parameters. Any publication of such weights must
retain the original authors, foundation model provenance, modification
details, and applicable terms.
https://github.com/zhangtaolab/Plant_DNA_LLMs
https://huggingface.co/zhangtaolab/plant-dnagpt-BPE
https://huggingface.co/zhangtaolab/plant-dnagpt-6mer

External models and services used by SalviaChat, including Ollama/Qwen and
BGE, as well as other external data and databases used by this project,
remain subject to their respective providers' terms. This repository does
not relicense those resources.

The bundled SalviaBench-Final-150.csv contains benchmark questions and gold
answers constructed from DeepSalviaDB database queries. Reuse of underlying
database content remains subject to its original terms.

When publishing results obtained with this project, also cite the original
resources actually used.
PDLLM paper: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molp.2024.12.006
STRING v12.0 paper: https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkad1000
